From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: Send a mouse move to the window under the cursor after show/hide.

AI-assisted (Claude), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream.

Windows 10 (x86_64 and i686, measured with
docs/wine-repro/server-mousemove-show-hide/measure.c, 2026-11-08): after a
window is shown, hidden, created, destroyed or moved, the window under the
cursor receives one WM_MOUSEMOVE, a burst of changes giving one, within
15-32 ms; a repaint alone gives none.

Wine sent none after show/hide, so Inventor's sketch showed an edited
dimension only after the mouse moved. Wine already sends one when a visible
window moves; this adds the show/hide case, delayed and coalesced.

The change is limited to visibility changes (moves are handled by Wine
already). WINE_SHOWHIDE_MOUSEMOVE_MS overrides the delay (0 disables it).

v2 (2026-11-08): the delay is 16 ms instead of 100 ms. With 100 ms the
move landed inside the next message sequence of Wine's own tests, which
pass on Windows (comctl32 button "expected WM_PAINT, got WM_MOUSEMOVE",
user32 test_mouse_input), in about half of the L2 runs.

v2 revised (2026-11-09, after cross review): the comment no longer says
the move arrives after the messages the change itself causes; the
measurement shows the delay and the coalescing, not the order of the
other messages.

v2 revised (2026-11-10, after the maintainer's L4 in Inventor 2027 with
the test-run/all-1 build): with 16 ms the sketch did not redraw after a
dimension edit until the mouse moved; WINE_SHOWHIDE_MOUSEMOVE_MS=16 and
24 failed, 32 and 100 worked. The default is now 32 ms, the upper end of
the delay Windows showed (15-32 ms, two timer ticks).

--- a/server/queue.c
+++ b/server/queue.c
@@ -589,6 +589,52 @@
     set_cursor_pos( desktop, desktop_shm->cursor.x, desktop_shm->cursor.y );
 }
 
+/* Windows sends the window under the cursor one mouse move after a window
+ * is shown, hidden, moved, created or destroyed, a burst of changes giving
+ * one move, within one or two timer ticks (15-32 ms measured). Inventor
+ * redraws its view after a sketch dimension edit only when that move
+ * arrives; under Wine it needs the upper end of that range (16 and 24 ms
+ * were too early, 32 ms works). */
+static struct timeout_user *cursor_pos_timeout;
+static struct desktop *cursor_pos_desktop;
+
+static void cursor_pos_timeout_cb( void *private )
+{
+    static const struct hw_msg_source source = { IMDT_UNAVAILABLE, IMO_SYSTEM };
+    struct desktop *desktop = cursor_pos_desktop;
+    struct message *msg;
+
+    cursor_pos_timeout = NULL;
+    cursor_pos_desktop = NULL;
+    if ((msg = alloc_hardware_message( 0xff515700, source, get_tick_count(), 0 )))
+    {
+        msg->msg = WM_MOUSEMOVE;
+        msg->x   = desktop->shared->cursor.x;
+        msg->y   = desktop->shared->cursor.y;
+        queue_hardware_message( desktop, msg, 1 );
+    }
+    release_object( desktop );
+}
+
+void update_cursor_pos_delayed( struct desktop *desktop )
+{
+    static int delay_ms = -1;
+
+    if (delay_ms < 0)
+    {
+        const char *env = getenv( "WINE_SHOWHIDE_MOUSEMOVE_MS" );
+        delay_ms = env ? atoi( env ) : 32;
+    }
+    if (!delay_ms) return;
+    if (cursor_pos_timeout)
+    {
+        remove_timeout_user( cursor_pos_timeout );
+        release_object( cursor_pos_desktop );
+    }
+    cursor_pos_desktop = (struct desktop *)grab_object( desktop );
+    cursor_pos_timeout = add_timeout_user( -(timeout_t)delay_ms * 10000, cursor_pos_timeout_cb, NULL );
+}
+
 /* retrieve default position and time for synthesized messages */
 static void get_message_defaults( struct msg_queue *queue, int *x, int *y, unsigned int *time )
 {
--- a/server/user.h
+++ b/server/user.h
@@ -124,6 +124,7 @@
 extern void set_clip_rectangle( struct desktop *desktop, const struct rectangle *rect,
                                 unsigned int flags, int reset );
 extern void update_cursor_pos( struct desktop *desktop );
+extern void update_cursor_pos_delayed( struct desktop *desktop );
 extern void post_message( user_handle_t win, unsigned int message,
                           lparam_t wparam, lparam_t lparam );
 extern void send_notify_message( user_handle_t win, unsigned int message,
--- a/server/window.c
+++ b/server/window.c
@@ -2770,6 +2770,8 @@
     if ((win->style & old_style & WS_VISIBLE) && (memcmp( &old_client, &win->client_rect, sizeof(old_client) )
         || memcmp( &old_window, &win->window_rect, sizeof(old_window) )))
         update_cursor_pos( win->desktop );
+    else if ((win->style ^ old_style) & WS_VISIBLE)
+        update_cursor_pos_delayed( win->desktop );
 
     if (win->paint_flags & SET_WINPOS_LAYERED_WINDOW) validate_whole_window( win );
 
